<title>GERMANY: Allianz Life says its shares undervalued.</title>
<headline>Allianz Life says its shares undervalued.</headline>
<dateline>DUSSELDORF, Germany 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Allianz Lebensversicherungs AG, the life unit of German insurer Allianz AG Holding, are significantly undervalued, the unit's chief financial officer said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no fundamental explanation for the share price. The figures look good and we have no skeletons in the closet,&quot; Karl-Hermann Lowe told an investor conference.</p>
<p>Allianz Leben stock last traded at 1,028 marks, well off their high for the year of 1,285 marks.</p>
<p>Lowe said around 10 percent of Allianz Leben stock was distributed among smaller investors.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
